<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY13-QA-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY13-QA-001" ;
  triage:title "crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs exceeds RULE-003 prod<=1000 line limit (prod=1042), hard CI lint gate failure" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1300-r1 (PR #1300, AY.13 doctor team scope, worktree pinned at 6189ad3f5). Live CI run 34145288398, job 'Just lint (ubuntu-latest)' (101815891095), step 'Run just lint' fails with exit code 1 at the 'lines' check: RULE-003 violation, active limits prod<=1000, crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs: prod=1042 exceeds limit 1000. Confirmed by direct local reproduction: python3 .just/check_line_counts.py in the pinned QA worktree reports the identical violation. Root cause: AY.13's D2 (DoctorTeamScope enum, per-team roster/presence/mixed-backend/graft-receiver looping) added the bulk of a 396-line diff in-place to crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs (git diff origin/integrate/phase-ay...6189ad3f5 shows +396/-71 for this file alone), pushing it from under the limit to 1042 production lines -- a genuine, reproducible hard CI gate failure introduced by this sprint's diff, not a pre-existing or flaky condition. Every other lint check (boundaries, fmt, clippy, adr-index, sc-boundary, pytests, etc.) passes at this head; this is exclusively the file-size RULE-003 gate. Fix requires splitting crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs (e.g. extracting the new DoctorTeamScope resolution/looping logic, or the presence_findings_for_team family, into a new sibling module under crates/atm-core/src/doctor/) to bring the file back under the 1000-line production cap; this is a structural split, not a logic change, and the sprint's existing D2/D3/D5 test coverage should transfer with it." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "lint-gate" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
